        "kind": "math",
        "text": "Point calculation: 4.355949 May anchor + 0.05 trend drift + 0.05 slack adjustment = 4.455949, rounded to a one-decimal first-print forecast of 4.5%. Interval calculation: center about 4.46 with half-width about 0.26 gives 4.19 to 4.72, reported as ciLow 4.2 and ciHigh 4.7."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Counter-considerations: upside risk is a June or July employment loss with participation holding near 66.7%, which would land above the interval. Downside risk is another May-like fall in unemployed people plus lower participation, which would land below the interval. A one-off rotation-group or survey-modernisation effect outside normal sampling variability could also push the first print outside the interval."
